---
import Main from "@/layouts/Main.astro";
import PageHeader from "@/components/PageHeader.astro";
import StatCounter from "@/components/StatCounter.astro";
import Placeholder from "@/components/Placeholder.astro";

const investment = [
  { nation: "United States", amount: "$280B", instrument: "CHIPS and Science Act", year: "2022" },
  { nation: "European Union", amount: "Multi-billion EUR", instrument: "EuroHPC Joint Undertaking", year: "2018-" },
  { nation: "United Kingdom", amount: "£1B", instrument: "AI infrastructure scheme", year: "2024" },
  { nation: "India", amount: "$1B", instrument: "IndiaAI", year: "2024" },
  { nation: "Canada", amount: "$2.7B", instrument: "AI Compute Access Fund + SCIP", year: "2024-26" },
];

const energy = [
  { province: "Quebec", cost: "$0.078/kWh", note: "Industrial as low as $0.05/kWh; cheapest in Canada" },
  { province: "Manitoba", cost: "$0.102/kWh", note: "Second cheapest; hydro-dominant" },
  { province: "British Columbia", cost: "$0.114/kWh", note: "Hydro-dominant" },
  { province: "Alberta", cost: "$0.258/kWh", note: "Deregulated; solar PPA below $30/MWh" },
];
---

<Main
  title="The Problem - Canada's compute sovereignty gap"
  description="Canada leads the G7 in AI talent but has no system in the global supercomputing top 50, and no mechanism for industry or citizens to build sovereign compute. The problem, with verified data."
  activePath="/problem"
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="The problem"
    title="World-leading talent. Zero sovereign compute for the people who need it."
    lede="Canada invested in AI talent without investing in the infrastructure that talent requires. The result is a compounding sovereignty crisis: talent trained here is commercialised elsewhere, because the infrastructure to retain it does not exist."
  />

  <!-- Problem 1: Infrastructure absence -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
    <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-spruce);">Problem 01 &middot; Infrastructure absence</p>
    <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight">
      Canada has no presence in the global supercomputing elite.
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        <p>
          The TOP500 list (November 2024) ranks the world&rsquo;s most powerful
          supercomputers. Canada does not appear in the top 10, which is
          dominated by the United States, Italy, Japan, Switzerland, and
          Finland. Canada&rsquo;s historical peak was roughly #110 (SciNet
          Niagara, 2018, now decommissioned).
        </p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-2 pl-5 text-ink" style="border-color: var(--color-spruce);">
          &ldquo;Currently, most compute capacity is located in other countries.
          Challenges accessing compute power slows down AI research and
          innovation, and also exposes Canadian firms to a reliance on
          privately-owned computing, outside of Canada. This comes with
          dependencies and security risks.&rdquo;
          <cite class="field-note mt-3 block not-italic text-graphite">
            Budget 2024, Chapter 4 (verbatim)
          </cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-hairline bg-parchment-2/40 p-7">
        <p class="field-label text-graphite">Sovereign compute investment</p>
        <table class="mt-4 w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-hairline text-left">
              <th class="pb-2 font-medium">Nation</th>
              <th class="pb-2 text-right font-medium">Committed</th>
              <th class="pb-2 text-right font-medium">Year</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              investment.map((r) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-hairline/60">
                  <td class="py-2.5">
                    <span class="font-medium text-ink">{r.nation}</span>
                    <span class="field-note block text-graphite/70">{r.instrument}</span>
                  </td>
                  <td class="py-2.5 text-right font-medium" style="color: var(--color-spruce);">{r.amount}</td>
                  <td class="field-note py-2.5 text-right text-graphite">{r.year}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="field-note mt-4 text-graphite/70">
          Canada&rsquo;s total commitment is roughly 1% of US investment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problem 2: talent-infrastructure disconnect -->
  <section class="border-y border-hairline bg-parchment-2/40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-spruce);">Problem 02 &middot; The talent-infrastructure disconnect</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight">
        Canada created demand for compute without creating supply.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-10">
        <StatCounter
          stats={[
            { value: "125+", label: "Canada CIFAR AI Chairs recruited", source: "Pan-Canadian AI Strategy" },
            { value: "1st", label: "in the G7 for AI publications per capita", source: "CIFAR" },
            { value: "3x", label: "the G7 average AI patent filing rate", source: "Budget 2024" },
            { value: "24,000", label: "researchers served, by academic allocation only", source: "Digital Research Alliance" },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        The talent is world-class. The infrastructure to support it is
        insufficient, and access runs through competitive academic allocation.
        Industry, startups, and junior researchers are structurally excluded.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problem 3: structural exclusion + CLOUD Act -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-spruce);">Problem 03 &middot; Structural exclusion</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          The whole private sector is pushed onto foreign clouds.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
          The national compute allocation model is designed exclusively for
          academic researchers. There is no pathway for startups, SMEs, or
          private companies to access public compute. This forces the private
          sector onto AWS, Azure, and GCP, which creates extraterritorial legal
          exposure under the U.S. CLOUD Act.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
          The CLOUD Act (2018) lets U.S. law enforcement compel U.S.-based
          providers to disclose data stored anywhere in the world, including
          Canadian data in a &ldquo;Canadian region.&rdquo; Geographic location
          is not legal jurisdiction. Canadian privacy law does not protect
          against this.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-spruce);">Problem 04 &middot; The energy paradox</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          The cheapest clean energy in the G7 sits disconnected from compute.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-6 border border-hairline bg-parchment p-6">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <tbody>
              {
                energy.map((e, i) => (
                  <tr class={i > 0 ? "border-t border-hairline" : ""}>
                    <td class="py-3 align-top">
                      <span class="font-medium text-ink">{e.province}</span>
                      <span class="field-note block text-graphite/70">{e.note}</span>
                    </td>
                    <td class="py-3 text-right align-top font-medium" style="color: var(--color-spruce);">{e.cost}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="field-note mt-4 text-graphite/70">
          Cold-climate cooling cuts data-centre cooling costs 40-60%. Quebec has
          700MW of surplus hydro. The assets exist; no mechanism aggregates them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Timeline placeholder -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline bg-parchment-2/40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-spruce);">How the gap opened</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight">
        A deliberate choice in 2017, acknowledged only in 2024.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        When Canada launched the world&rsquo;s first national AI strategy in
        2017, it chose to invest in algorithms and talent, assuming access to
        foreign compute would follow. The bet was wrong. By the time the gap was
        acknowledged in Budget 2024, the U.S. had committed a hundred times more
        capital to the problem.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10">
        <Placeholder
          kind="data"
          ratio="21/9"
          label="Timeline: Canada's AI compute infrastructure decisions, 2000-2026"
          note="Sourcing brief: horizontal timeline in four eras (Foundation 2000-16, Talent Strategy 2017-21, Awakening 2022-24, Response 2025-26). Source data in context/three-ws.md. Dossier styling, mono labels, spruce markers on decision points."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Evidence integrity note -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl border-l-2 pl-6" style="border-color: var(--color-spruce);">
      <p class="field-label text-graphite">On the numbers</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        Every figure on this page is traceable to a primary government,
        institutional, or peer-reviewed source. Where a commonly cited statistic
        could not be verified against a primary source (for example, specific
        talent-emigration percentages), we have left it off rather than repeat
        it. Credibility is the point.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 text-center lg:px-10">
      <h2 class="mx-auto max-w-2xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
        The problem is real, verified, and government-acknowledged. Here is the mechanism.
      </h2>
      <a
        href="/how-it-works"
        class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center px-7 py-3.5 text-sm font-medium text-white transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
        style="background-color: var(--color-spruce);"
      >
        How DAI Compute works
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Main>
